                <pb facs="0126" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg18"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in inclosure 1 in No.
                        13.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gelletich to Mr.
                            Hammond.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consular Agency of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Fiume</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                                1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Born 1871; emigrated 1885; naturalized 25th October, 1892; passport dated Vienna
                    15th April, 1893, No. 379; too young to be summoned before emigration; to-day he
                    leaves for Pola to be soldier. Urgent protection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gelletich.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
